<section class="content-section" id="overview-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <h2 class="section-title">12A Registration in Gurugram - Overview</h2>
            <div class="content-text">
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-bottom:20px;">
                    <p><strong>&#128204; TL;DR - 12A Registration in Gurugram Services at a Glance</strong></p>
                    <p>12A registration exempts your NGO's surplus income from income tax under the Income Tax Act, 1961. Without 12A, every rupee of surplus above expenses is taxed at normal rates. Registration is filed online through the IT e-filing portal using Form 10A (provisional, 3 years) or Form 10AB (regular/renewal). Post-2025 amendment: small trusts with income up to Rs 5 crore can get 10-year validity on renewal. For Gurugram NGOs targeting CSR funding from the Fortune 500 corridor in Cyber City and Udyog Vihar, 12A is the non-negotiable first step.</p><div class="table-responsive-wrapper" style="margin-top:16px;"><table><thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Governing Law</td><td>Income Tax Act, 1961 - Section 12A / 12AB</td></tr><tr><td>Authority</td><td>PCIT (Exemptions), Delhi</td></tr><tr><td>Portal</td><td>incometax.gov.in (e-filing portal)</td></tr><tr><td>Forms</td><td>Form 10A (provisional/new) | Form 10AB (regular/renewal)</td></tr><tr><td>Validity</td><td>Provisional: 3 years | Regular: 5 years | Small trusts (&le;Rs 5Cr): 10 years (post-March 2025)</td></tr><tr><td>Govt Fee</td><td>NIL - no government fee</td></tr><tr><td>Benefit</td><td>NGO surplus income fully exempt from income tax</td></tr><tr><td>CSR Relevance</td><td>Mandatory for CSR funding under Section 135, Companies Act 2013</td></tr></tbody></table></div></p>
                </div>
                <p>Gurugram is home to India's densest concentration of Fortune 500 companies - DLF Cyber City, Udyog Vihar, Golf Course Road, and Sohna Road house offices with combined CSR obligations running into hundreds of crores annually under Section 135. For NGOs targeting this corporate ecosystem, 12A is the gateway to the CSR pipeline. The regulatory framework has changed since Finance Act 2020 - all registrations are now time-bound. A critical 2025 amendment extends renewal to 10 years for small trusts. Learn more about <a href="#">12A/80G Registration across India</a>.</p>
                <p>Patron Accounting's Gurugram office on Golf Course Extension Road provides end-to-end 12A registration bundled with <a href="/ngo-registration">NGO Registration</a>, 80G (donor deduction), NGO Darpan, CSR-1, and <a href="/accounting-services">Accounting Services</a> for annual compliance - the complete NGO tax compliance package for Gurugram's CSR corridor.</p>
                <p>Content is reviewed quarterly for accuracy.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- SECTION 3: WHAT IS GSTAT APPEAL FILING -->
<section class="content-section" id="what-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">What Is 12A Registration</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p>12A registration is the process by which a charitable or religious trust, society, or Section 8 company obtains income tax exemption on its surplus income under Sections 12A and 12AB of the Income Tax Act, 1961, by filing Form 10A (provisional) or Form 10AB (regular) with the Principal Commissioner of Income Tax (Exemptions).</p><p>Once registered, the NGO's income applied towards charitable purposes is fully exempt under Sections 11 and 12. Donations received, interest on corpus, rental income from trust property, and any other income used for charitable objects are not taxed. Without 12A, the same income is taxed at applicable slab rates.</p><p>For Gurugram-based NGOs, 12A unlocks not just tax exemption but also CSR contributions from companies in Cyber City, Udyog Vihar, and the Golf Course Road corporate corridor - most of whom mandate 12A as a funding prerequisite.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for 12A Registration in Gurugram:</strong></p>
                    <p><strong>Section 12A/12AB:</strong> Original provision requiring registration for income tax exemption. Section 12AB (post-Finance Act 2020) is the current operative section. All registrations are time-bound.</p><p><strong>Form 10A:</strong> Provisional 12A registration for new NGOs. 3-year validity. Filed on IT e-filing portal.</p><p><strong>Form 10AB:</strong> Regular or renewal registration. 5-year validity (10 years for small trusts with income &le; Rs 5 Cr post-March 2025). Filed 6 months before expiry.</p><p><strong>PCIT(E) Delhi:</strong> Principal Commissioner of Income Tax (Exemptions) - processes 12A for all Haryana NGOs including Gurugram.</p><p><strong>Section 2(15):</strong> Defines 'charitable purpose' - relief of the poor, education, yoga, medical relief, preservation of environment/monuments, advancement of general public utility.</p><p><strong>10-Year Validity (2025 Amendment):</strong> Small trusts with income &le; Rs 5 crore in each of preceding two years get 10-year renewal validity. Filed after March 31, 2025.</p>

                </div>
            </div>
