            <div class="content-text">
                
                <p><strong>Charitable Trusts:</strong> Registered with Sub-Registrar, Gurugram under Indian Trusts Act, 1882. Operating in education, healthcare, poverty alleviation, environment. Without 12A, surplus donations and grants are taxed. Trusts working with CSR teams in DLF Cyber City cannot receive funding without valid 12A.</p><p><strong>Societies:</strong> Registered under Haryana Registration and Regulation of Societies Act, 2012 with District Registrar, Gurugram. Educational, cultural, welfare, and charitable bodies need 12A for income exemption. Patron bundles 12A with society registration.</p><p><strong>Section 8 Companies:</strong> Non-profit companies with RoC Delhi. Highest CSR credibility among corporate donors. 12A essential within first year. Preferred by Cyber City corporates for CSR partnerships.</p><p><strong>Religious Trusts with Charitable Activities:</strong> Temples, gurudwaras with charitable wings (education, medical relief, feeding). Objects must be clearly defined in trust deed for 12A eligibility.</p><p><strong>Existing NGOs Needing Renewal:</strong> 5-year registrations from 2021 expired March 2026. Missed September 2025 deadline for Form 10AB means lapsed status. Patron provides urgent remediation with condonation-supported filing.</p>

