                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-1">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How do I get 12A registration for my Gurugram NGO?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>File Form 10A on the income tax e-filing portal (incometax.gov.in) for provisional 12A. Upload trust deed or MOA, PAN, activity report, and address proof. PCIT (Exemptions) Delhi processes the application. Provisional registration is valid for 3 years. Patron's Gurugram office handles the complete filing and PCIT scrutiny response.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-2">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is Section 12A of the Income Tax Act?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Section 12A (read with Section 12AB post-2020) requires charitable trusts, societies, and Section 8 companies to register with the Income Tax Department to claim income tax exemption under Sections 11 and 12. Without 12A, the NGO's surplus income is taxed at normal rates. Registration is via Form 10A (provisional) or Form 10AB (regular/renewal).</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-3">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What documents are needed for 12A registration?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>PAN of NGO, trust deed or MOA/AOA, registration certificate, activity report, governing body details with PAN and Aadhaar, and Gurugram registered office address proof. For Form 10AB (regular), audited financial statements for the last 3 years are additionally required. Patron prepares all documents before filing.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-4">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Is 12A registration mandatory for NGOs?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>While not technically mandatory to operate, without 12A your surplus income is taxed like a business. CSR donors in Gurugram's Cyber City and Udyog Vihar will not fund NGOs without valid 12A. Government grants and FCRA eligibility also depend on 12A status. Effectively non-negotiable for any serious charitable organisation.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-5">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How long does 12A registration take?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Provisional via Form 10A takes 15-30 working days. Regular via Form 10AB takes 30-90 working days depending on PCIT(E) scrutiny. Timeline extends if PCIT raises queries. Patron monitors applications daily and responds within the 30-day window to minimise delays.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-6">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is Form 10A vs Form 10AB for 12A?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Form 10A is for new or provisional 12A registration - grants 3-year validity. Form 10AB is for converting provisional to regular, or renewing existing registration - grants 5-year or 10-year validity depending on income threshold. Both filed on IT e-filing portal. Patron determines the correct form based on your NGO's history.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-7">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Can a new NGO apply for 12A immediately?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Yes. New trusts, societies, and Section 8 companies can apply immediately after incorporation via Form 10A. No financial history required for provisional. The 3-year provisional must be converted to regular via Form 10AB before expiry. Patron files 12A within 15 days of NGO registration.</p></div>
